  "details": "Vive Advanced Control used to have a unique mechanic that would allow the user to only press once on their left controller's trackpad so that they can move forward/back and strafe without the need to make additional inputs. I am currently using the instructed binds for Vive since the update and it does not do this.\n\nFor clarity on what I mean.\n\nBefore the Update:\n\n1. Press once anywhere on the trackpad while keeping your thumb on the trackpad\n\n2. Move your thumb around with visible results for moving forward, back, left and right.\n\nAfter the Update:\n\n1. Same instruction as before\n\n2. Moving thumb around does not doing anything for movement, requiring you to press again on the trackpad to move or strafe.\n\nThe reason why I find this removed functionality important for the Vive controllers is so that it doesn't damage the trackpad over time due to over-use. It also makes using the Vive controllers comfortable to use, rather than being an annoyance to control for long periods of time.",
